<!-- Appearance: the sun-and-moon mark, traced from the supplied artwork.

     One filled disc, its moon taken out of it by a second circle laid over the
     first and a third laid inside that, three craters punched through the
     crescent, and six round-capped rays standing off the rim — two vertical, four
     at the diagonals. Every number here is the drawing's own, measured off the
     512 px source and mapped into this 24-unit box at 24/432; the shape is the
     shape, not an impression of it.

     It is one colour so the row can tint it like every other mark in the page,
     and the holes are holes rather than paper-coloured discs, so it reads on
     cream by day and on charcoal at night without a second file. -->
